        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #40223.">Fix</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3207089235" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40223" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40223/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40223">#40223</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Apparently I keep merging XSLT guides: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2997386030" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39141" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/39141/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39141">#39141</a>, <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2840433846" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38057" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/38057/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/38057">#38057</a>. After this one we have a single guide as opposed to 6 that talk about the same thing...</p>
<p dir="auto">I'm ignoring all the intro in the DOM API guide. This information is all present in the XSLT guide article, and in a more elaborate fashion.</p>
<p dir="auto">I'm moving the DOM API guide into the XSLT guide, because in fact these examples don't invoke JS at all, so it shouldn't belong in the API docs. It was only there because it was originally in <code class="notranslate">XSLTProcessor</code> and I was only looking to improve IA at that time.</p>]]></content>
